Escritorio Digital: licensing

This repository combines two layers of work, under two licenses.

1) UPSTREAM LAYER: clodfarm, under the MIT License (LICENSES/MIT-clodfarm.txt).
   Copyright (c) 2026 Duke Security, Inc.
   Everything that comes from https://github.com/matank001/clodfarm and was not changed by us stays under the MIT License.
   This repository does not narrow that license.

2) OUR LAYER: PolyForm Shield License 1.0.0 (LICENSES/PolyForm-Shield-1.0.0.md).
   Required Notice: Copyright (c) 2026 lcssurf (https://github.com/lcssurf/escritorio-digital)

   It covers the files and folders that are new in this project:
     overlay/                    the desktop app (characters, panel, texts)
     scripts/escritorio.mjs      the install and maintenance tool
     clodfarm/team.py            the team: chief, leads and specialists
     clodfarm/chat.py            conversation with the team and the plan
     clodfarm/progress.py        following a job: who called whom, what each one is doing
     tests/test_team.py, tests/test_chat.py, tests/test_ux.py,
     tests/test_landing_approval.py, tests/test_claude_connectors.py, tests/test_licenses.py, tests/test_progress.py, tests/test_review_edit.py
     INSTALAR.md, CLAUDE.md, NOTICE.md, TRADEMARKS.md, Dockerfile.dev

   and OUR CHANGES to these files that came from clodfarm (the unchanged upstream parts of each remain MIT;
   `git diff 95e5841 HEAD -- <file>` shows exactly what we changed):
     Dockerfile, .dockerignore, README.md, pyproject.toml,
     clodfarm/auth.py, clodfarm/cli.py, clodfarm/config.py, clodfarm/gitops.py, clodfarm/policy.py,
     clodfarm/store.py, clodfarm/supervisor.py, clodfarm/web.py, plugins/farm/lib/clodfarm/policy.py

In short (this is a summary, the license texts control): you may use Escritorio Digital, including inside a business,
for any purpose, except to provide a product or service that competes with it. See the Shield license for the exact
definition of "compete". The copyright holder can grant other terms in writing.

Names, logos and the look of the characters are not licensed: see TRADEMARKS.md.
Claude Code, which the container image includes, is Anthropic's software, under Anthropic's terms: see NOTICE.md.
